.IX Title "GENCANCEL 1"
.TH GENCANCEL 1 2023-04-16 "INN 2.7.4" "InterNetNews Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
gencancel \- Generate cancel control messages
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBgencancel\fR [\fB\-adkLm\fR] [\fB\-b\fR \fIbody\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcharset\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIfrom\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR \fInewsgroups\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fIsubject\fR] \fImessage-id\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBgencancel\fR provides the news administrator with a helpful tool to generate
cancel control messages, writing them to standard output.  The generated
cancel article can then be injected by \fBinews\fR (see examples below).
.PP
\&\fBgencancel\fR expects the Message-ID of the article to cancel; this
\&\fImessage-id\fR argument should properly be quoted for the shell and surrounded
by angle brackets.  \fBgencancel\fR will then try to read the original article
in the news spool to determine the original newsgroups it was posted to, and
re-use that information for the cancel control message.  If you want to modify
that, or if the information was not found, you'll have to set it with the
\&\fB\-n\fR flag.
.PP
If INN was built with Cancel-Lock support, \fBgencancel\fR will generate the
right admin Cancel-Key header field to use in order to authenticate cancels.
If, for whatever reason, you need cancelling an article posted from your news
server with a Cancel-Lock header field, the corresponding admin Cancel-Key
hashes are needed to authenticate the withdrawal request.  That information is
computed with the \fIcanlockadmin\fR parameter set in \fIinn\-secrets.conf\fR.
.PP
In case you only need the admin Cancel-Key hashes, you can use the \fB\-k\fR flag.
Only the body of the Cancel-Key header field will then be written to standard
output.  You can then re-use it for instance in a supersede request or from
another script.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP \fB\-a\fR 4
.IX Item "-a"
\&\fBgencancel\fR outputs by default an Approved header field, using the same value
as the From header field body.  If \fB\-a\fR is used, no Approved header field
is output.
.Sp
This header field is useful for cancelling articles originally posted to
moderated newsgroups.  If a cancel control article lists a moderated newsgroup
in its Newsgroups header field, and no Approved header field is present,
the cancel will be sent to the moderator first for approval.  Cancel control
messages are not required to contain an Approved header field outside of
moderated newsgroups, but can, so you shouldn't generally use \fB\-a\fR unless
you really want your cancels to be approved by a moderator, or are sure the
Newsgroups header field does not list any moderated newsgroups.
.IP "\fB\-b\fR \fIbody\fR" 4
.IX Item "-b body"
\&\fBgencancel\fR writes by default \f(CW\*(C`Admin cancel.\*(C'\fR in the body of cancel control
messages.  Using this argument permits writing a different value, which may be
empty or multi-line.
.IP "\fB\-c\fR \fIcharset\fR" 4
.IX Item "-c charset"
By default, \f(CW\*(C`ISO\-8859\-1\*(C'\fR is specified as the used charset in the Content-Type
header field.  In case you change the default body with \fB\-b\fR, you may want to
also change \fIcharset\fR accordingly.
.IP \fB\-d\fR 4
.IX Item "-d"
\&\fBgencancel\fR generates a Date header field in the local time of your news
server.  Using \fB\-d\fR will make use of a UTC date.
.IP "\fB\-f\fR \fIfrom\fR" 4
.IX Item "-f from"
\&\fBgencancel\fR uses by default the value of \fIcomplaints\fR in \fIinn.conf\fR for the
From header field.  Using this argument permits setting the value you want.
The same value will be used for the Approved header field (if generated, when
\&\fB\-a\fR is not given).
.IP \fB\-k\fR 4
.IX Item "-k"
Instead of outputting a whole cancel control message, \fBgencancel\fR will just
output the body of the Cancel-Key header field with admin hashes.
.Sp
This flag is only available if INN was built with Cancel-Lock support.
.IP \fB\-L\fR 4
.IX Item "-L"
\&\fBgencancel\fR outputs by default a Cancel-Key header field to authenticate
the cancel control message.  If \fB\-L\fR is used, no Cancel-Key header field is
output.
.Sp
This flag is only available if INN was built with Cancel-Lock support.
.IP \fB\-m\fR 4
.IX Item "-m"
\&\fBgencancel\fR generates by default a random Message-ID and uses it as unique
identifier of the cancel control message.  If \fB\-m\fR is used, no Message-ID
header field is output.
.IP "\fB\-n\fR \fInewsgroups\fR" 4
.IX Item "-n newsgroups"
\&\fBgencancel\fR generates by default the same Newsgroups header field as the one
present in the original article to cancel.  This is done to best ensure that
the cancel control message will be relayed to the same news servers as the
original message.
.Sp
In case your news server does not (or no longer) locally carry the
original article, you will have to give an explicit newsgroup or list of
comma-separated newsgroups with this flag, that will be used as the Newsgroups
header field of the cancel.
.IP "\fB\-s\fR \fIsubject\fR" 4
.IX Item "-s subject"
\&\fBgencancel\fR uses by default \f(CW\*(C`cmsg cancel <message\-id>\*(C'\fR as the subject
of cancel control messages.  Using this argument permits setting a different
value for the Subject header field.  Make sure it is properly MIME-encoded.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
To only retrieve the admin Cancel-Key hashes associated to the given
Message-ID:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    gencancel \-k \*(Aq<mid@news>\*(Aq
.Ve
.PP
If you're using non-ASCII characters in headers, make sure you properly
MIME-encode them.  For instance, use the \f(CW\*(C`Encode\*(C'\fR Perl module:
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    FROM=$(perl \-e \*(Aquse Encode;
\&                    print encode("MIME\-Q",
\&                                 decode("UTF\-8", "Julien ÉLIE"));\*(Aq)
\&    gencancel \-f "$FROM <admin@news.server.com>" \*(Aq<mid@news>\*(Aq
.Ve
.PP
You'll then see in the output a properly MIME-encoded header field:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    From: =?UTF\-8?Q?Julien_=C3=89LIE?= <admin@news.server.com>
.Ve
.PP
An example of call with a custom multi-line body:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    gencancel \-b "$(echo \-e "Multi\enLine\enBody.")" \*(Aq<mid@news>\*(Aq
.Ve
.PP
(Use \fB\-c\fR to change the default Content-Type charset for the body.)
.PP
You can then pipe the result into \f(CW\*(C`inews \-h \-P \-D\*(C'\fR (meaning \fBinews\fR expects
an article with headers, does not add a Sender header field, and writes the
result to standard output instead of actually injecting it):
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    gencancel \*(Aq<mid@news>\*(Aq | inews \-h \-P \-D
.Ve
.PP
If it all looks good, then inject it into the news system (without giving
\&\f(CW\*(C`\-D\*(C'\fR to \fBinews\fR):
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    gencancel \*(Aq<mid@news>\*(Aq | inews \-h \-P
.Ve
.PP
Note that \fBinews\fR sends the message to the server specified in the \fIserver\fR
parameter in \fIinn.conf\fR.
.SH "تاریخچه (HISTORY)"
.IX Header "HISTORY"
Written by Julien Élie for InterNetNews.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
